{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffRMxyN2FFB6Y6BcF2tX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate passed the self-check: it printed `OK`, with a finite ELPD-LOO of −2257.4 from the short smoke fit. That number isn't comparable to the incumbent's −2317.6. It comes from 100 draws on one chain, and 10.9% of trials had high Pareto k, so the smoke fit's LOO estimate is flagged unreliable. R-hat can't be computed from one chain, so convergence, novelty against the live models and the 30-minute speed limit will only be tested at admission.\n\n**Model chosen:** `tally_span_ideal_plus_switch_reward` (rank 1, 49.6 ± 15.0 nats behind the best). Its mechanism is closest to the incumbent's, but its reward for switching is linear, which is exactly what the critique faults.\n\n**The one change:** switching is no longer rewarded without limit. Each sequence is judged by how close its switching rate is to a shared ideal rate, so the reward rises and then falls (prior favours an ideal above one half). More switching looks more random only up to that rate, and perfect alternation like HTHTHTHT looks too regular. People differ in how much this weighs. Everything else is kept from the original: the running heads-minus-tails tally, each person's expected tally span, the length-scaled sensitivity and the personal left/right lean.\n\n**Why:** two of the discrepancies that survive the FDR correction come from the linear switching reward:\n- People choose the perfect alternator less often than predicted (0.532 observed vs 0.598 predicted).\n- Among pairs where both sequences switch often, people choose the more-switching one at a different rate than predicted (0.525 vs 0.465).\n\nThe change doesn't address the third, people favouring sequences with more distinct three-flip chunks.\n\n**Name:** `tally_span_switch_rate_ideal`\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_5/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3436,"cache_read_input_tokens":76043,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3436,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bde64ab7-d974-4071-b165-ca1505051caa","uuid":"7a5d46e1-afc9-4ec0-9d94-dec4e59d76a8","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:57:36.295Z","request_id":"req_011CffRMxZ4FZB3SWJVAKgZQ"}
